You didn't pick any defaults to reopen, so I acknowledged all three as they stand:
- one branch and PR per issue;
- no changelog entries for repository tooling;
- `eval-export.sh` only if week 1 needs it.

Defaults don't write atoms, so nothing new lands in `.kb/`. This session's ledger has nothing open or unreviewed now, so the container can go without losing anything (D-0014).

The only open item from this session is [#61](https://github.com/Wet-Ink-Corporation/weigh-in/pull/61), the board defaults cap. I'll report when its CI finishes.

The tag now points at `868b4bb Release 0.5.2 (#71)`, and the release run for it is going ([run 8](https://github.com/Wet-Ink-Corporation/weigh-in/actions/runs/37238570116)). The earlier run on the wrong commit stopped at the version check and published nothing.

I've set a check-in for 22:13 UTC. Then I'll look at:
- the run's result;
- the release assets: the zip, the three binaries and `SHA256SUMS`;
- the new `marketplace` commit: version 0.5.2, `weighin.exe` executable, hooks in exec form, and the new convention line in the binary.

Two of the three follow-up items are done or running:

- **Eval seed:** done and committed locally on `temper/remediation`, not pushed yet. I added five of this session's end-of-turn messages to `eval/seed.jsonl` (`rs10-01` to `rs10-05`). Three are captured as logged defaults and two are true negatives. On the real seed, precision stays at 100% and recall goes from 40% to 54%, and the `eval_seed` test passes. The README has a matching paragraph.
- **Code follow-ups:** still running in the background, each with a review pass. They cover:
  - rolling back when `COMMIT` fails, at both sites in the store;
  - a fixed date for the receipt test, using the assertion change you approved;
  - Miri skip markers on every test that starts the binary or git;
  - logging hook input failures only inside a git repo.

When the follow-ups land I'll run the gate, push to PR 82 and update its description. After that I'll run `/weigh-in` to settle this session's calls, so the follow-up fixes can close three of them first.
